# ── Discord Presence Bridge (Railway service, server-only) ─────
# Secrets. Never commit values. Never reuse the website's OAuth
# credentials here — this service uses a BOT token, which must never
# appear in Vercel, the browser, GitHub, or logs.

# Bot token from Discord Developer Portal → Bot → Reset Token.
# SECRET. Railway → service → Variables only.
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# Owner to watch. Defaults to the site owner; set explicitly anyway.
# Not secret (it is displayed on the website itself).
# DISCORD_USER_ID=920627516694200360

# A server where BOTH the bot and the owner are members. The bot
# needs no admin permissions — plain membership is enough.
# Find it: Server Settings → Widget → Server ID (enabling the widget
# itself is NOT required), or enable Developer Mode → right-click
# server → Copy Server ID.
# DISCORD_GUILD_ID=

# Shared secret for GET /presence (Vercel proves itself with
# `Authorization: Bearer <this>`). SECRET. Minimum 32 characters.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# Must match DISCORD_PRESENCE_BRIDGE_SECRET on the website exactly.
# PRESENCE_SHARED_SECRET=

# Railway injects PORT automatically; keep the default locally.
# PORT=3000
